  "interpretation": {
    "corners": "The two end features occupy different stone courses. Image bearings constrain horizontal coordinates only. Absolute station georeferencing is approximate. The ray residuals describe internal agreement and do not incorporate common coordinate or camera offsets. Allow metre-scale uncertainty in absolute placement.",
    "courtyard": "Three of four pediment apexes and the projecting front edge of a balcony were matched across three street views. The apexes sit approximately 12.4–12.8 m back from the north reference line. The balcony edge sits at about 11.9 m. Cornice and balcony projections put these features at different offsets from the wall.",
    "west_end": "The restored red-brick north front meets later hotel work at the street corner identifiable in three views. The modern hotel masks the western termination of the historic courtyard wall. Its exact length, west wall return and junction with the hotel remain unmeasured.",
    "east_end": "The southeastern masonry turn of the recessed end projects roughly 1.14 m west and 11.33 m into the block from the northeast stone base. A dark interval separates the historic red masonry and the hotel facade in the southeastern view."
  }
